[
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 1,
      "ps": "P1-S1"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 1,
      "id": "P1-S1",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "When prehistoric man arrived in new parts of the world, something strange happened to the large animals: they suddenly became extinct.",
    "translation": "当史前人类到达世界新的地方时，大型动物发生了一些奇怪的事情：它们突然灭绝了。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": true,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 2,
      "ps": "P1-S2"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 2,
      "id": "P1-S2",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "Smaller species survived.",
    "translation": "较小的物种幸存下来。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": true
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 3,
      "ps": "P1-S3"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 3,
      "id": "P1-S3",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "The large, slow-growing animals were easy game, and were quickly hunted to extinction.",
    "translation": "这种体型大、生长缓慢的动物很容易被猎杀，但很快就被猎杀至灭绝。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 4,
      "ps": "P1-S4"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 4,
      "id": "P1-S4",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "Now something similar could be happening in the oceans.",
    "translation": "现在海洋中也可能发生类似的事情。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 5,
      "ps": "P1-S5"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 5,
      "id": "P1-S5",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "That the seas are being overfished has been known for years.",
    "translation": "多年来，人们都知道海洋正在被过度捕捞。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 6,
      "ps": "P1-S6"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 6,
      "id": "P1-S6",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "What researchers such as Ransom Myers and Boris Worm have shown is just how fast things are changing.",
    "translation": "兰塞姆·迈尔斯 (Ransom Myers) 和鲍里斯·沃姆 (Boris Worm) 等研究人员已经证明，事情的变化速度有多快。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "sentence": 7,
      "ps": "P1-S7"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 7,
      "id": "P1-S7",
      "pIndex": 1
    },
    "text": "They have looked at half a century of data from fisheries around the world.",
    "translation": "他们研究了半个世纪以来世界各地渔业的数据。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 1,
      "ps": "P2-S1"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 1,
      "id": "P2-S1",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "Their methods do not attempt to estimate the actual biomass (the amount of living biological matter) of fish species in particular parts of the ocean, but rather changes in that biomass over time.",
    "translation": "他们的方法并不试图估计海洋特定部分鱼类的实际生物量（活生物物质的数量），而是估计该生物量随时间的变化。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": true,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 2,
      "ps": "P2-S2"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 2,
      "id": "P2-S2",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "According to their latest paper published in Nature, the biomass of large predators (animals that kill and eat other animals) in a new fishery is reduced on average by 80% within 15 years of the start of exploitation.",
    "translation": "根据他们在《自然》杂志上发表的最新论文，新渔业中大型捕食者（杀死并吃掉其他动物的动物）的生物量在开始开发后的 15 年内平均减少了 80%。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": true
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 3,
      "ps": "P2-S3"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 3,
      "id": "P2-S3",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "In some long-fished areas, it has halved again since then. Dr. Worm acknowledges that these figures are conservative.",
    "translation": "在一些长期捕捞的地区，此后又减半了。沃姆博士承认这些数字是保守的。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 4,
      "ps": "P2-S4"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 4,
      "id": "P2-S4",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "One reason for this is that fishing technology has improved.",
    "translation": "造成这种情况的原因之一是捕鱼技术的进步。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 5,
      "ps": "P2-S5"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 5,
      "id": "P2-S5",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "Today's vessels can find their prey using satellites and sonar, which were not available 50 years ago.",
    "translation": "如今的船只可以利用卫星和声纳来寻找猎物，而这在 50 年前是无法实现的。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 6,
      "ps": "P2-S6"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 6,
      "id": "P2-S6",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "That means a higher proportion of what is in the sea is being caught, so the real difference between present and past is likely to be worse than the one recorded by changes in catch sizes.",
    "translation": "这意味着海洋中捕获的鱼的比例更高，因此现在和过去之间的真正差异可能比捕获量变化记录的差异更严重。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "sentence": 7,
      "ps": "P2-S7"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 7,
      "id": "P2-S7",
      "pIndex": 2
    },
    "text": "In the early days, too, longlines would have been more saturated with fish.",
    "translation": "在早期，延绳钓中的鱼也更加饱和。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "sentence": 1,
      "ps": "P3-S1"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 1,
      "id": "P3-S1",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "Some individuals would therefore not have been caught, since no baited hooks would have been available to trap them, leading to an underestimate of fish stocks in the past.",
    "translation": "因此，有些个体不会被捕获，因为没有诱饵鱼钩来捕获它们，导致过去低估了鱼类种群。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": true,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "sentence": 2,
      "ps": "P3-S2"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 2,
      "id": "P3-S2",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "Furthermore, in the early days of longline fishing, a lot of fish were lost to sharks after they had been hooked.",
    "translation": "此外，在早期的延绳钓中，很多鱼被鲨鱼上钩后丢失。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": true
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "sentence": 3,
      "ps": "P3-S3"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 3,
      "id": "P3-S3",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "That is no longer a problem, because there are fewer sharks around now. Dr. Myers and Dr. Worm argue that their work gives a correct baseline, which future management efforts must take into account.",
    "translation": "这不再是问题，因为现在周围的鲨鱼越来越少了。迈尔斯博士和沃姆博士认为，他们的工作提供了正确的基线，未来的管理工作必须考虑到这一点。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "sentence": 4,
      "ps": "P3-S4"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 4,
      "id": "P3-S4",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "They believe the data support an idea current among marine biologists, that of the \"shifting baseline\".",
    "translation": "他们认为这些数据支持海洋生物学家中流行的一个观点，即“基线移动”。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "sentence": 5,
      "ps": "P3-S5"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 5,
      "id": "P3-S5",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "The notion is that people have failed to detect the massive changes which have happened in the ocean because they have been looking back only a relatively short time into the past.",
    "translation": "人们的观点是，人们未能察觉海洋中发生的巨大变化，因为他们只回顾了相对较短的过去。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
    },
    "provenance": {
      "sourceLayer": "production",
      "sourceFile": "题库/英语/data_2006.js",
      "year": 2006,
      "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
      "extractedAt": "2026-09-18T23:13:00+0800",
      "contentHash": "sha256:dae9dbb471cf116cef828c941e47f18acef37c8c20398cd3fd6bb0126f995932"
    }
  },
  {
    "schemaVersion": "kaoyan-existing-sentence-1.0",
    "source": "production",
    "articleKey": "ky-en1-2006-r-t3",
    "location": {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "sentence": 6,
      "ps": "P3-S6"
    },
    "sourceLocator": {
      "sIndex": 6,
      "id": "P3-S6",
      "pIndex": 3
    },
    "text": "That matters because theory suggests that the maximum sustainable yield that can be cropped from a fishery comes when the biomass of a target species is about 50% of its original levels.",
    "translation": "这很重要，因为理论表明，当目标物种的生物量约为其原始水平的 50% 时，渔业可实现最大可持续产量。",
    "syntaxAnalysis": null,
    "rawFields": {
      "isTopicSentence": false,
      "isKeyEvidence": false
